    "notes": "Second fix pass: every two-line shot now has 8 words or fewer (lines of 3 to 5 words, holds 0.1) so no shot can reach 5 s; the 5.3 s shot survived the first fix because only the button was split. Fix pass: split the 3-line button into two shots and trimmed long lines so every shot stays under 4.5 s. Real kitty scene: the late friend who shares a live location while the gang waits, and the gang reads her excuses against the map. One want (Tanya wants Avika and the halwa now), one game (each excuse busted by the dot), played ordinary (traffic at a petrol pump), ordinary (signal called Glow Parlour), absurd (she is buying the carrots). Claim before reveal: Avika says the halwa is ekdum ready one shot before the mandi stop. Twist is a see-it cooker in her hands in the doorway. Button repeats her opening line and the opening chip at 8:45 pm, so it loops. Avika is the late one per the bible and her catchphrase Traffic tha yaar appears once. Rewrote the ending twice: first she brought shop-bought halwa (no flip), then she handed everyone graters (needs a prop we do not have and slows the end). Kind humour: nobody is mocked, the halwa does arrive."
